#: ../../source/docs/common-3d-mapping.rst:108
#: c72e27f388304a54ae275781ddcb7fff
msgid "All of these software packages work in generally the same way in that they consume the still images you've taken from the vehicle (and you may also choose to add pictures taken by hand from the ground as well) and produce a 3d image (in what format?).  This is accomplished by automatically matching up the images, it does not rely upon knowing the actual location from where the image was taken."
msgstr ""

